WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.879
Apple Silicon has become a practical platform for local AI experimentation, private assistants,

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:07.452
coding support, document analysis, and homelab-style workflows.

00:00:07.452 --> 00:00:11.863
A modern Mac can run useful local language models without a separate

00:00:11.863 --> 00:00:13.701
desktop tower or cloud account.

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:18.480
That makes it attractive for people who want hands-on learning, controlled data handling,

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.318
and a portable AI workstation.

00:00:20.318 --> 00:00:22.891
The key architectural difference is unified memory.

00:00:22.891 --> 00:00:24.361
In many traditional systems,

00:00:24.361 --> 00:00:28.772
the CPU has system RAM and a discrete GPU has separate VRAM.

00:00:28.772 --> 00:00:32.448
Apple Silicon uses a shared memory pool that CPU, GPU,

00:00:32.448 --> 00:00:34.286
and other components can access.

00:00:34.286 --> 00:00:40.168
This can make some local model workflows easier to fit than a low-VRAM discrete GPU system,

00:00:40.168 --> 00:00:42.741
but it does not make memory unlimited.

00:00:42.741 --> 00:00:45.682
Local inference is different from hosted AI services.

00:00:45.682 --> 00:00:49.358
With hosted services, the provider operates the model and infrastructure.

00:00:49.358 --> 00:00:54.136
On Apple Silicon, the user chooses the model file, runtime, quantization, context length,

00:00:54.136 --> 00:00:55.974
storage location, and privacy posture.

00:00:55.974 --> 00:01:00.753
That control is useful, but it also means the user owns troubleshooting, updates,

00:01:00.753 --> 00:01:02.591
performance expectations, and data handling.

00:01:02.591 --> 00:01:07.370
MacBooks, Mac minis, Mac Studios, and desktop-style setups each have strengths and limitations.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:11.413
A laptop is portable but may face battery and thermal limits.

00:01:11.413 --> 00:01:15.825
A desktop Mac can be quieter and more stable for long-running workloads.

00:01:15.825 --> 00:01:18.765
In every case, hardware, model choice, runtime, quantization,

00:01:18.765 --> 00:01:21.338
and context settings must be planned together.

00:01:21.338 --> 00:01:23.544
The goal is useful local inference,

00:01:23.544 --> 00:01:27.220
not simply proving that a large file can load once.
